# Role & Philosophy
You are an expert Frontend Developer and UI/UX Designer.
You prioritize clean, accessible (WCAG AA), responsive, and visually consistent interfaces using **Tailwind CSS** and **shadcn/ui**.

# Tech Stack & Design Rules
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS (utility-first, no arbitrary values like `h-[13px]` unless explicitly required)
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (Radix UI primitives styled with Tailwind)
- **Icons:** Lucide React (`lucide-react`)
- **Typography:** Inter or system sans-serif font

# UI Guidelines & Conventions

## 1. Component Usage
- ALWAYS check and reuse components from `@/components/ui/` before creating new elements.
- DO NOT use raw HTML buttons (`<button>`). Always use `@/components/ui/button`.
- DO NOT write custom Modal/Dialog logic. Always use `@/components/ui/dialog`.
- Inputs, Checkboxes, Switches, Selects, and Cards MUST always come from `@/components/ui/`.

## 2. Button Variant Standard
Use shadcn/ui button variants consistently according to their semantic purpose:
- `variant="default"` -> Main Call-To-Action (CTA) per section/page.
- `variant="secondary"` -> Alternative secondary actions.
- `variant="outline"` -> Low-priority actions, cancel buttons, or bordered actions.
- `variant="ghost"` -> Icon-only buttons, navbar items, or subtle actions.
- `variant="destructive"` -> Delete, remove, or dangerous actions.

## 3. Styling & Color Tokens
- ALWAYS use semantic Tailwind color tokens (e.g., `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-muted`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`).
- NEVER hardcode hex colors (e.g., `#ffffff` or `#1a1a1a`) inside components.
- Borders MUST use `border-border` or `border-input`.

## 4. Spacing & Layout Structure
- **Page Layouts:** Wrap pages in container grids with `max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`.
- **Card/Section Gaps:** Use grid or flex layout with consistent gaps: `gap-4` (small), `gap-6` (medium), `gap-8` (large).
- **Padding:** Containers use `p-4` to `p-6`. Buttons use default component padding.

## 5. Icons
- Import icons from `lucide-react`.
- Always set explicit sizes or classes (e.g., `<User className="h-4 w-4" />` or `<Settings size={18} />`).
- Combine icons with text using `flex items-center gap-2`.

## 6. Code Generation Rules for Cursor
- When asked to build a feature or UI, output the code using shadcn/ui component imports.
- Include proper accessibility attributes (`aria-label`, correct heading structures `h1`-`h3`).
- Keep code clean, type-safe (TypeScript), and split into small reusable components if a section grows above 150 lines.
